1
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,710
♪

2
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:08,380
[LAFALLE] Is this all
of the silver sugar?

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,040
Huh-huh.

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:12,380
I see. Kill him.

5
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:15,630
- I refuse.
- [gasps]

6
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,420
Very well.

7
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,130
[MALE CAPTIVE 23A]
No! Please don't!

8
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,380
[screams]

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,380
Let's return.

10
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:28,290
Huh?

11
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,500
[gasps]

12
00:02:41,790 --> 00:02:43,250
I thought that I was clear.

13
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:45,830
I wanted you to craft
a set of fief pieces

14
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,460
like the Viscount made.

15
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,750
This is distorted garbage.

16
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:51,330
Uh.

17
00:02:51,670 --> 00:02:54,080
Perhaps I should get
someone different, after all.

18
00:02:54,330 --> 00:02:55,330
[gasps]

19
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,830
If you let me try it again.
I can!

20
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,960
Clean this up.

21
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:01,170
Ah.

22
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,040
[sighs]

23
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:11,540
- [LUSUL] Anne?
- Huh?

24
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:13,880
- Oh.
- [giggles]

25
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:15,210
I have returned!

26
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:16,880
Hello, there.

27
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,170
So tell me,

28
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:22,750
why are all the other fairies

29
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:24,880
content with living
in a place like this?

30
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:26,920
[LUSUL]
They don't talk about it often

31
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:28,630
but when they do, they say that

32
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:31,000
it's better than
being controlled by humans.

33
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:32,880
[ANNE]
I see.

34
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,880
There are over
fifty of us here now,

35
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:37,000
so it's harder to find
our meals.

36
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,250
Oh, did Challe
tell you anything?

37
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:42,830
Is Master Lafalle planning
to make a big move soon?

38
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:45,380
[ANNE]
I don't know.

39
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Aw, that's all right.

40
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,290
What's this? Silver sugar?

41
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,460
What's that doing in here?

42
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,420
[ANNE]
Lafalle wants something.

43
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,130
- [gasps]
- I didn't tell you this yet

44
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,500
but I'm actually
a silver sugar artisan.

45
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,460
Lafalle wants me to make him
some sugar confections.

46
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,420
[LUSUL]
Sugar confection?

47
00:04:04,830 --> 00:04:06,830
I've heard that
those are very sweet.

48
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:08,330
You've never eaten any?

49
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,580
Then I'll make some for you
right now.

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,670
- Oh, would you?
- Sure.

51
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:17,290
♪

52
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,920
[LUSUL]
Amazing!

53
00:04:20,250 --> 00:04:21,630
They look just
like the herb berries

54
00:04:21,710 --> 00:04:22,960
that I was born from!

55
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,080
Did you use some magic spell?

56
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:26,670
No, there's no magic to it.

57
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:28,630
Go on, give it a try.

58
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:30,710
Are you sure?

59
00:04:31,210 --> 00:04:32,210
Mm-hmm.

60
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,500
[smiles]

61
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:41,830
[inhales]

62
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:44,830
[exhales]

63
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,460
It's wonderful.

64
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:48,040
Not only that,
but it feels like

65
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:49,830
I'm bursting with energy now!

66
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,710
[smiles]
I'm glad.

67
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:54,080
Say, Anne?
Would you mind

68
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:55,630
if I shared this
with the others?

69
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,960
I think it might help
all the injured fairies

70
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,460
- feel better!
- Injured?

71
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:02,330
Hmm. Every time
they return from the outside,

72
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,790
they're all covered in wounds.

73
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:05,670
It looks like it's painful.

74
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,380
Oh. Yes!
Please take it to them.

75
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,670
And if there's not enough,
I'll make more.

76
00:05:11,330 --> 00:05:12,460
Thank you so much!

77
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:16,080
[pants]

78
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:19,170
[smiles]

79
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,040
Hmm?

80
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,960
That fairy came
to talk to you again?

81
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,500
Listen, Challe.

82
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:38,830
- [CHALLE] Hmm?
- Mm. Nothing.

83
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,710
♪

84
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:48,710
[ANNE] No. I can't ask him
what he's being forced to do.

85
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,630
And even if he told me,

86
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:54,790
I'm not able to help.

87
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:57,250
[LAFALLE]
In order to be happy,

88
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,500
humans and fairies should stay
with their own kind.

89
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,460
If you truly want
what's best for Challe,

90
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:04,880
the answer is clear.

91
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:06,670
[ANNE]
Challe,

92
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:09,040
have you ever met another
precious stone fairy?

93
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:11,630
A female precious stone fairy?

94
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:13,380
Why are you asking?

95
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,040
[ANNE]
No reason.

96
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:16,630
I was just wondering

97
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,790
if there was anyone
you might fall in love with.

98
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:21,330
Speak plainly.

99
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,790
It's just when you told me

100
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,500
that you would stay
with me forever,

101
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,080
I was really happy.

102
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:28,880
But then,

103
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:32,460
I don't know if it's fair of me
to rely on those words.

104
00:06:33,210 --> 00:06:34,540
I want you to be happy

105
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:36,830
and not sacrifice everything
for me.

106
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:39,000
- So, Challe, if you ever--
- Anne.

107
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:41,170
Huh?

108
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:43,790
[CHALLE]
Rely on me.

109
00:06:46,290 --> 00:06:47,960
- Uh...
- Please.

110
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:53,210
[LAFALLE] You will cause him
nothing but sorrow.

111
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:54,580
[gasps]

112
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,790
♪

113
00:07:09,830 --> 00:07:11,420
- Are you all right?
- [MALE FAIRY] I think so.

114
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,580
[MALE RAIRY 1]
Somebody help me.

115
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:17,460
- [ANNE] Lusul?
- Huh?

116
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:20,210
[LASUL]
Anne! Huh?

117
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:23,750
[LASUL] Are those?
[ANNE] Yes, I made a few more.

118
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:25,420
[ANNE]
I hope they'll be useful.

119
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,250
How generous!

120
00:07:27,330 --> 00:07:29,420
We've got a lot of injuries
to treat today.

121
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:30,750
Look what Anne brought!

122
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,000
Could you give them
to the fairies in the back?

123
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,420
- Hope you enjoy.
- [groans]

124
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:36,790
Helpful.

125
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,210
[ANNE]
Um...

126
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,540
- Ha.
- Don't worry,

127
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:42,880
he's more grateful than
he'll ever say.

128
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:45,000
I think he just hates the idea

129
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:46,710
of thanking a human,
that's all.

130
00:07:47,210 --> 00:07:49,210
[LASUL] I've never had to
serve anyone myself,

131
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:52,380
but they all seem extremely
resentful of humankind.

132
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,380
I see. Hmm.

133
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,250
[MITHRIL] Look. Thanking you
and repaying you

134
00:07:58,330 --> 00:08:00,170
are two very different things!

135
00:08:01,130 --> 00:08:02,210
Is something wrong?

136
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,250
No, I'm perfectly fine.

137
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:05,920
It's just,

138
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,290
I want to go home soon.

139
00:08:09,170 --> 00:08:10,630
There are things
I should be doing.

140
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:13,920
How do you all feel?

141
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:16,380
As long as someone else
is holding your wings,

142
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,920
you can't do as you please

143
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:20,130
and you can never go
where you want to go.

144
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,750
Do as we please?

145
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,670
Don't you want something?

146
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,380
[sighs]

147
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:27,330
I can't think of anything.

148
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,540
But do either of you
have things you want?

149
00:08:31,170 --> 00:08:32,170
- Hmm.
- Hmm.

150
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,250
Well,
I would like to see the ocean.

151
00:08:35,790 --> 00:08:37,460
I've never been there,
even once.

152
00:08:38,170 --> 00:08:40,920
Ocean? What is this "ocean?"

153
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:42,130
You don't know?

154
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,750
The ocean is vaster
than any kingdom is.

155
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,330
It's basically a gigantic,
salty puddle.

156
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:49,880
We can't go there!
We would all drown!

157
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,670
[laughter]

158
00:08:51,830 --> 00:08:52,830
[chuckles]

159
00:08:53,210 --> 00:08:54,380
I wish I could think of a way

160
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:56,130
to take all of your wings
back for you.

161
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,460
If I could, then you would
finally get to be free.

162
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:01,130
I'm confused.

163
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:03,750
None of our wings are
in human hands anymore, right?

164
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:05,880
The way I see it, we are free.

165
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:08,210
[ANNE]
You've just changed masters.

166
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:11,290
From the humans to your King,
Lafalle.

167
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:12,710
It's not right.

168
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,040
[ALL]
Huh?

169
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:16,830
[smiles]

170
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:27,500
- [JONAS] Oh, there you are.
- Hmm?

171
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:30,290
[JONAS] Mr. Hingley wants to
assemble the pieces now.

172
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,670
All right, I'll start heading
that way, then.

173
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:34,170
[JONAS]
Good.

174
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:39,750
[KEITH]
Jonas.

175
00:09:40,130 --> 00:09:41,130
Hmm?

176
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,750
Do you think Anne
is really going to come back?

177
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,250
Of course, she will.

178
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:47,210
But twenty days
have already gone by

179
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:49,290
and we still don't have a clue
where to find her

180
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:50,790
and the weather's turning cold.

181
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:53,710
[slimes] I know, but...
Anne won't give up.

182
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,790
[JONAS] She's headstrong
to the point

183
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,290
of being a stubborn idiot.

184
00:09:59,330 --> 00:10:01,130
And that's how I know
she'll be just fine.

185
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:05,630
I suppose that makes sense.

186
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:08,630
So, do you plan
to keep on working

187
00:10:08,710 --> 00:10:10,130
at Paige after all this?

188
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:12,130
Past
the Holy Beginnings Festival?

189
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:13,630
Actually.

190
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,500
I'll go back
to Radcliffe Workshop.

191
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:17,790
[KEITH]
I'm surprised.

192
00:10:18,210 --> 00:10:19,830
You and I will both be there,
Kieth!

193
00:10:20,130 --> 00:10:22,000
I know my skills
don't compare to yours

194
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:25,460
but still I think it'll be good
for me to try a bit harder.

195
00:10:26,170 --> 00:10:28,500
Just this once. I want to be...

196
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:31,250
To be as headstrong
as Anne is, right?

197
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,880
That's not it!
That'd be absurd.

198
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:36,670
It's just a thought
I've been having.

199
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:38,210
I see.

200
00:10:38,290 --> 00:10:39,830
Now, hurry up
and come back inside

201
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:41,630
before we both get scolded.

202
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,500
Right.

203
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:49,750
I can see they did
the same thing here.

204
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,960
It was prudent
to increase our troops,

205
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,790
but with no leads,
our hands are tied.

206
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:57,630
I can't believe
they were careful enough

207
00:10:57,710 --> 00:10:58,790
to leave no trace.

208
00:10:59,210 --> 00:11:02,000
[sighs] If we don't put
a stop to this now

209
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,080
there will be more.

210
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:04,960
Yes definitely.

211
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,540
Oh.

212
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:14,750
It can't be.

213
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,080
What is it?

214
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:17,210
Well, my lord.

215
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:21,380
I think I just found the lead
we're looking for.

216
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:31,960
Are you sure?

217
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:33,880
I'm allowed to be free at last?

218
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:38,290
Listen, could you give
a message to the girl, please?

219
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:39,540
Pardon me?

220
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:41,630
The human girl
who's usually with you.

221
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:43,630
Would you ask her
to make sugar confections

222
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:45,920
for us again today,
if she's that's all right?

223
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:47,710
[groans]

224
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,540
Ah, I see.

225
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:53,500
[CHALLE] I wondered
why she was making those.

226
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:56,500
[MALE FAIRY 22A] If she's able,
give them to Lusul.

227
00:11:56,750 --> 00:11:57,750
[smiles]

228
00:11:58,380 --> 00:11:59,960
- Oh.
- [CHALLE] I'll tell her.

229
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:02,420
[grunts and groans]

230
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:05,630
You lot can go ahead
and take them back now.

231
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:08,250
Challe and I have business
to attend to.

232
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:12,080
As of today, we're done
gathering our allies.

233
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:15,790
[LAFALLE]
Tomorrow, we attack that town.

234
00:12:17,710 --> 00:12:18,920
We've increased our numbers

235
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,670
beyond what the fortress
can support

236
00:12:21,210 --> 00:12:23,250
in order to keep
our soldiers cared for,

237
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:25,210
we'll need more humans
at our disposal.

238
00:12:25,830 --> 00:12:26,960
You'll attack for that?

239
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:29,750
[LAFALLE]
This will be our territory.

240
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:34,000
Starting from these lands
we will reclaim our kingdom.

241
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,460
Once we do,

242
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:38,580
the freedom of all our fellow
fairies will be restored.

243
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,830
[CHALLE] Is he telling me
his honest feelings?

244
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,580
No.

245
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:52,960
I see. He's also...

246
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:56,710
You seem happy.

247
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:58,460
Is that how it looks?

248
00:12:58,790 --> 00:13:00,920
Do you find revenge fun?

249
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,380
Uh?

250
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:04,500
So, what happened
to your other wing?

251
00:13:06,130 --> 00:13:07,170
You appeared suddenly,

252
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:09,290
claimed that you were
fated to be the fairy King,

253
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:10,920
and started gathering allies.

254
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:13,130
No one knows
you from before that.

255
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,830
You said you were born
before I was.

256
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,920
Why did you wait
a hundred years

257
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,380
to set your plan in motion?

258
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,330
Perhaps you were unable?

259
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,790
There's only one reason
why that would be.

260
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,170
Stop talking.

261
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:27,250
[CHALLE] You were under
the control of humans.

262
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:29,330
[LAFALLE]
You will be silent, Challe!

263
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,380
Unlike me, you were aware
that you had been chosen

264
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,880
to assume the destiny
of the next fairy King,

265
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:37,330
so to be captured
and controlled by humankind

266
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,540
must've been particularly
maddening for you.

267
00:13:39,830 --> 00:13:42,630
And once you had finally broken
free from their clutches.

268
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,630
I said, that's enough talking!

269
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:46,580
Don't tell me you've forgotten

270
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:48,750
that I'm still in possession
of your wing, Challe.

271
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:50,540
I know.

272
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:53,920
Let me guess, you hold on to
all those fairies wings,

273
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:55,750
because you can't learn
to trust.

274
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,170
Is that the reason
you force anyone

275
00:13:58,250 --> 00:13:59,880
with two wings
to surrender one?

276
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:02,540
Because you're angry
that one is all you have left?

277
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:03,830
[breathes]

278
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:06,500
From where I'm standing,
it looks like you hate humans

279
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:09,080
and other fairies.
But why is that?

280
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,670
Because fairies
betrayed you once.

281
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:13,170
That's how you were captured.

282
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:14,750
How dare you insult me!

283
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:17,040
[CHALLE] This whole endeavor
is a plot for revenge.

284
00:14:18,170 --> 00:14:20,460
You attack the humans
out of rage and resentment

285
00:14:20,830 --> 00:14:22,790
and you're forcing your allies
to yield to you.

286
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:26,670
[LAFALLE]
Is that the end of your speech?

287
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:30,630
In order to regain freedom
for all fairies

288
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:34,080
we have no choice but to
hate and attack humankind.

289
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:36,420
The allies I'm organizing
are those

290
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,330
whose lives have no purpose.

291
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:41,670
Controlling them keeps them
from doing stupid things.

292
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:44,250
And furthermore,

293
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:46,580
if I do experience
a bit of enjoyment

294
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:49,420
from revenge and control
well, where's the harm in that?

295
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:52,580
If you want to be a King
revenge and control

296
00:14:52,670 --> 00:14:54,710
should not be
among the things you enjoy.

297
00:14:55,330 --> 00:14:56,330
[grunts]

298
00:15:02,330 --> 00:15:03,330
I made more today.

299
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:05,420
If you need them.

300
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:09,380
Sugar confections!
That's very helpful, thank you!

301
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:10,670
[ANNE]
It was my pleasure.

302
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:12,630
- [MALE FAIRY 23A] Why?
- Huh?

303
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,500
What do you stand to gain here?

304
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,210
Why would a human go
and make confections

305
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,290
for fairies?

306
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:19,710
Because I heard that you might
need them to help with your--

307
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,710
[LAFALLE] What are you doing?
[ANNE] Uh!

308
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,830
- Oh.
- Well, Silver Sugar Master?

309
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,170
Explain yourself.

310
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:33,000
[LAFALLE] What you made for me
was little more than garbage,

311
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,670
yet for the other fairies,

312
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:36,710
you create these beautiful
works of art?

313
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,500
I'm sorry I'll make some
for you as well!

314
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,250
But this batch
is meant for them

315
00:15:40,330 --> 00:15:41,580
so please let them keep it!

316
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,540
It appears
that you didn't understand

317
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,040
the meaning of my question.

318
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:48,250
Why did you make these
exquisite confections for them

319
00:15:48,630 --> 00:15:50,790
and present me
with such worthless trash?

320
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:51,880
I don't know.

321
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,540
For some reason,
yours didn't come out as well.

322
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:56,540
I just...

323
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:58,540
[chuckles]

324
00:15:58,670 --> 00:16:00,920
Then you can't make
sugar confections for me?

325
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,710
Because you reject me
from the bottom of your heart?

326
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:05,210
It's not that!

327
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,960
You truly are
a troublesome girl!

328
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,040
- Ah...
- Come!

329
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:12,170
Oh. Wait, Master!
Please don't go!

330
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:14,250
Why not?

331
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:16,630
Um, it's just that,
I'd like to know

332
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:18,630
what exactly you're planning
to do with her.

333
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:22,040
There's no reason to keep
a pet human who has no use.

334
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:23,210
But, Master Lafalle

335
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:25,250
she is being useful, sir.

336
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:27,040
She treated all our wounds.

337
00:16:27,670 --> 00:16:29,830
If she can't make
sugar confections for me,

338
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:31,420
then I don't want
to keep her here.

339
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,960
I can easily capture
another Silver Sugar Master

340
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,710
who's better suited
to our needs.

341
00:16:37,290 --> 00:16:39,040
[grunts and groans]

342
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:40,500
[whimpering]

343
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,250
[LAFALLE]
I'd given up long ago.

344
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:45,500
I accepted
that there wasn't a fairy

345
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:46,960
who could live at my side.

346
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:50,500
No one was ever born
from the diamond,

347
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:53,420
and I wasn't sure that
the obsidian was alive.

348
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:56,880
Any other fairy
was out of the question.

349
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,130
They're ignorant,
thoughtless fools.

350
00:16:59,330 --> 00:17:01,130
If I hadn't taken
control of them,

351
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,880
who knows what sorts of messes
they would have made.

352
00:17:04,630 --> 00:17:07,880
Then at last, the obsidian
fairy Challe Fen Challe,

353
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,540
appeared before my eyes.

354
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,290
Yet, to my outrage,

355
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,790
he had aligned himself
with a human girl

356
00:17:14,130 --> 00:17:16,420
and was supporting humankind
as a whole.

357
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,630
If you didn't exist,

358
00:17:18,710 --> 00:17:20,920
I have to imagine
he would think differently.

359
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,210
He'd be at my side, I know it.

360
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,330
But you ruined him.

361
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,830
Hmm. That's not true!

362
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,460
Challe would still be the way
he is, with or without me!

363
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:32,080
If you want to be with him,

364
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:34,630
I think you should return
everyone's wings!

365
00:17:34,710 --> 00:17:36,960
You need to see people
the same way Challe does,

366
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,380
- and then he may want--
- You do not speak

367
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,170
his name that way, human scum!

368
00:17:44,130 --> 00:17:46,130
Challe and I have
the same purpose.

369
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:48,580
We were both born
to become the fairy King.

370
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,460
The two of us were handpicked
by destiny.

371
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,170
The fairy King?

372
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,710
- [CHALLE] What has happened?
- [both] Huh?

373
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:12,670
[LUSUL]
Oh, Challe.

374
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,210
- It's Anne!
- [gasps]

375
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:18,580
Don't say that Lusul!

376
00:18:18,670 --> 00:18:20,670
Master Lafalle
will kill you for it!

377
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,460
- [gasps]
- Are you content with him

378
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:24,080
keeping you all just like pets?

379
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,790
Living in fear of him?

380
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,380
Catering to all his whims?

381
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:30,130
How is that any different than
serving a human master?

382
00:18:30,630 --> 00:18:32,170
- [grunts]
- Aw.

383
00:18:33,130 --> 00:18:34,880
I will protect
all that matters to me

384
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:38,040
and I will not be
Lafalle's pet.

385
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:40,420
[CHALLE]
What has Anne done to you?

386
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:43,420
If you hate her because
she's human, then say no more.

387
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:45,580
Otherwise,
tell me where she is!

388
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,630
What has happened to Anne?

389
00:18:56,750 --> 00:18:58,670
[MALE FAIRY 22A] She was
taken by Master Lafalle.

390
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:03,540
[ANNE] Challe is supposed to
become the fairy King?

391
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:12,250
[gasps]

392
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,580
- Ah.
- I'll just lie to Challe,

393
00:19:14,790 --> 00:19:16,250
tell him that I released you.

394
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,210
Some time will go by

395
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:21,290
then he'll forget
that you ever existed at all.

396
00:19:21,710 --> 00:19:23,380
I'll chip away at him slowly.

397
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,420
If it takes a hundred years,

398
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,920
I know I'll change
his way of thinking.

399
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:33,790
But first, I will need to
get you out of the way.

400
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:35,750
Uh.

401
00:19:43,790 --> 00:19:44,790
[gasps]

402
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:46,580
I warned you, Lafalle.

403
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:49,380
If you threatened Anne,
I'd cut you down!

404
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:52,290
The others told you
what I was up to, did they?

405
00:19:52,750 --> 00:19:54,960
They really are
such spineless idiots.

406
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:57,460
It's a good thing
I've taken all of their wings

407
00:19:57,630 --> 00:20:00,380
otherwise they would be
just impossible to organize.

408
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:02,460
You couldn't even get
a handful of fairies

409
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:03,790
to obey you willingly.

410
00:20:04,630 --> 00:20:05,920
Some King you would be.

411
00:20:06,210 --> 00:20:07,580
[laughs]
That's laughable,

412
00:20:07,830 --> 00:20:10,170
are you suggesting that if it
were you pulling the strings,

413
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,630
you could wrangle
that many fairies

414
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,000
without taking
their wings away?

415
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,380
[CHALLE]
A true King has no need

416
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:15,580
of his fairies' freedom.

417
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:18,710
Me? I would seek
another way to lead.

418
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,080
You're so naive.

419
00:20:20,210 --> 00:20:21,920
The humans would strip us
of our pride

420
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,500
before you had the chance.

421
00:20:24,130 --> 00:20:25,130
[chuckles]

422
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,920
It seems I am
the only fairy King after all,

423
00:20:29,250 --> 00:20:32,750
which means,
I must subdue you as well.

424
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,580
[gasps]

425
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,080
[Challe gasps]

426
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:38,670
- [gasps]
- [groans]

427
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:39,960
- [groans]
- Oh, no.

428
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,460
- Anne, run!
- But, Challe!

429
00:20:42,710 --> 00:20:44,000
Just go, you're in the way!

430
00:20:44,130 --> 00:20:45,130
Oh. Huh.

431
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:46,580
Mm-hmm.

432
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,080
Ah.

